description:
The README's Config table (the rows '| `key` | default | what |' under '## Config') and bead-loop.example.toml document the keys Repo::load reads in src/config.rs (cfg.str/u64/bool calls: label, merge, merge_label, setup, gate, on_exhaust, conflict_worker, brief_model, adopt, max_inflight, worker_timeout, attach, model, review_model, base; plus repos, stages, lanes read by Layers). Nothing checks that they agree; a key added to config.rs can go undocumented.

Add one #[test] in the existing mod tests of src/config.rs (no new files, no new dependencies) that:
- lists the key names as a const slice in the test: ["repos", "lanes", "label", "base", "setup", "gate", "model", "review_model", "stages", "on_exhaust", "conflict_worker", "brief_model", "merge", "merge_label", "adopt", "max_inflight", "worker_timeout", "attach"];
- reads README.md with include_str!("../README.md") and asserts each key appears as a table row: the README text contains the string "| `KEY` |" (for stages and lanes the row is "| `[[stages]]` |" and "| `[[lanes]]` |");
- reads bead-loop.example.toml with include_str!("../bead-loop.example.toml") and asserts each key except repos and lanes (global-only) appears at the start of a line, optionally after '# ', as "KEY =" or "[[KEY]]";
- asserts the other direction for the README: every "| `name` |" row in the Config table names a key in the slice (parse lines between '## Config' and the next '## ', take lines starting with '| `', strip the backticks and any '[[ ]]'), so a documented key that config.rs stopped reading fails too.
The assertion messages name the missing key and the file.
